{
  "dom_id": "step-q336466",
  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "The data below is taken from the table of values of the cumulative distribution function $Φ(z)$ for the standard normal distribution. Given that $X∼N(6,{3}^{2}),$ compute $P(7.26<X<8.85).$ Use the tables below and do not round your answer.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.00\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.01\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.02\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.4\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6554\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6591\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6628\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.5\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6915\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6950\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.6985\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.6\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7257\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7291\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.7324\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"5\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr> <th width=\"25%\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$z$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.05\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.06\\,$</th><th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.07\\,$</th>\n</tr><tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,0.9\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8289\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8315\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8340\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.0\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8531\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8554\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8577\\,$ </td></tr>\n<tr> <th bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$\\,1.1\\,$</th><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8749\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8770\\,$ </td><td align=\"center\"> $\\,0.8790\\,$ </td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n$P(7.26<X<8.85)=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Given a normal random variable $X∼N(\\mu ,{\\sigma }^{2}),$ we have\n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)=P(\\frac{a-\\mu }{\\sigma }<Z<\\frac{b-\\mu }{\\sigma })\n$$\n\nwhere $Z∼N(0,1)$ is a standard normal random variable. In our case, we have $\\mu =6$ and $\\sigma =3.$\n\nFirst, we transform $X$ into a standard normal random variable $Z$ by $z$-scoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(7.26<X<8.85) & =P(\\frac{7.26-6}{3}<Z<\\frac{8.85-6}{3}) \\\\  & =P(0.42<Z<0.95).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe required probability is represented by the area shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14263116/assets/39f9ac74ed4f39708f882116edb554b15051ea820e4b5ea8a38e5451ed706251.png)\n\nNow, we express the required probability in terms of $Φ(z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.42<Z<0.95) & =P(Z<0.95)-P(Z\\le 0.42) \\\\  & =P(Z\\le 0.95)-P(Z\\le 0.42) \\\\  & =Φ(0.95)-Φ(0.42).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the table, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.95) & =0.8289 \\\\ Φ(0.42) & =0.6628\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0.42<Z<0.95) & =Φ(0.95)-Φ(0.42) \\\\  & =0.8289-0.6628 \\\\  & =0.1661.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we conclude that\n\n$$\nP(7.26<X<8.85)=0.1661.\n$$",
